00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.630 align:start position:0%
the General Affairs Council on the 17th  of March will prepare for the March EU  summit where the main focus will be to  set up the establishment of an energy  union ministers will review proposals  included in the commissioners ng union  strategy a key EU priority the goal is  to make the European Union market more  competitive more sustainable and to  ensure a secure supply of energy the  council will also lay the groundwork for  heads of state and government to review  the first phase of the European semester  4 2015 the European semester is a  process under which EU countries agree  on economic and fiscal policy priorities  for a given year the blocks leaders are  expected to provide guidance to member  states for the preparation of their  national reform and stability or  convergence programmes finally ministers  will review external relations issues  ahead of the leaders meeting these will  include preparations for the may 2015  Eastern Partnership summit in Riga as  well as relations with Russia and the  situation in Ukraine regarding the  latter talks will focus on the  implementation of the Minsk agreement  and possible further steps the situation  in Libya has implications for the  security of the European Union is also  on the agenda
 

